Q: How to generate a random string of a fixed length in Go? A: <p>In Go 1.24, the <code>crypto/rand</code> package now has the <code>Text()</code> function which uses uppercase letters and provides 128bit of randomness (26 characters):</p>
<pre class="lang-golang prettyprint-override"><code>package main

import (
    &quot;crypto/rand&quot;
    &quot;fmt&quot;
)

func main() {
    randstr := rand.Text()  // &lt;-- here
    fmt.Println(randstr)
}
</code></pre>
<p>Result:</p>
<pre><code>NKZBIM6DTFN2R4QBH4HRNY6NCM
</code></pre>
